<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Faustin Soulouque</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1782">1782</a>–<a href="/years/1867">1867</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Faustin I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Faustin Soulouque was a Haitian general chosen president by the senate in 1847 as a supposedly pliable figure. He purged the mixed-race elite, proclaimed himself Emperor Faustin I in 1849 and built a lavish court. His repeated invasions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-republic">Dominican Republic</a> were defeated, and he was overthrown by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fabre-geffrard">Fabre Geffrard</a> in 1859 and went into exile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/faustin-soulouque.jpg" alt="Faustin Soulouque" width="320" height="523" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Faftylo80 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emperor_Faustin_I_Ha%C3%AFti.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
